00-first: reading="I want to keep track of the books I've read this year because I usually forget what I read by december, I can see all the books I've read this year in one place, with a short note about what I thought of each one, so I can remember and review my reading more easily. It works if I can find each book I've read this year and its short note in one place; It should be nothing fancy." focused=null
00-first: reading="I'm worried our onboarding emails are annoying people, while marketing values them, I can decide whether and how to change the first-week onboarding emails without eliminating them entirely, so I want new users not to feel spammed while preserving useful marketing value. I don't want to kill the emails entirely, and they must not make new users feel spammed." focused={"id":"model-8e04ab2098d0cddc","text":"What would convince you that the onboarding emails are no longer causing an unacceptable annoyance?"}
00-first: reading="When learners answer a question incorrectly, especially on phones, they currently see a red X and may leave, I can I want learners leaving a wrong answer feeling smarter, not dumber, by understanding why their answer was wrong, so People may feel dumb and leave, and I want to reduce that drop-off. It has to work on phones. No gamification. I should not assume an AI chat panel or a rebuilt quiz engine is the solution." focused={"id":"model-187a327b310f4c26","text":"What would show you that a learner feels smarter after a wrong answer?"}
