00-first: reading="When I’m tired at night, talking is faster than typing, and opening a terminal feels like work, I can determine whether I need voice input, an easier way to start dumps, or both, so I can make starting a dump feel less effortful." focused={"id":"model-2f42041f2f103850","text":"Do you mainly want to identify the biggest source of friction, or design a way to start nighttime dumps despite both frictions?"}
00-first: reading="I am trying to work on a system that compounds itself and serves as a meta harness for coordinating work across the entire continuum of agentic software development lifecycle, I can take work from a brain dump, prompt, hunch, or intuition through a cohesive, rigorous, durable, verified change to a PR ready for human review, so The system helps me consider the health of the whole codebase—the forest, not just the trees—and makes the next change easier. I want a human-first system in which I am the restaurateur who tastes the final product; rigor, durability, cohesion, and verification should all just work." focused={"id":"model-41f5423370ee7c8b","text":"What would let you know that this system is achieving its true goal?"}
